Repair the following TypeScript module and return one corrected complete source file.

`averageBuckets(values, bucketSize)` must return the arithmetic mean of each consecutive bucket, including a final partial bucket. An empty input returns an empty array. Reject a bucket size that is not a positive integer with `RangeError`, and reject non-finite values with `TypeError`. Preserve input order and do not mutate or alias the input. The current implementation incorrectly loses data in a boundary case.

```typescript
export function averageBuckets(
  values: readonly number[],
  bucketSize: number,
): number[] {
  if (!Number.isInteger(bucketSize) || bucketSize <= 0) {
    throw new RangeError("bucketSize must be a positive integer");
  }
  if (values.some((value) => !Number.isFinite(value))) {
    throw new TypeError("values must be finite");
  }

  const result: number[] = [];
  for (let start = 0; start <= values.length - bucketSize; start += bucketSize) {
    const end = Math.min(start + bucketSize, values.length);
    let sum = 0;
    for (let index = start; index < end; index += 1) {
      sum += values[index];
    }
    result.push(sum / (end - start));
  }
  return result;
}
```

